---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Articles | Data Engineering, Cybersecurity & Technology | Federica Iengo" description="Technical articles by Federica Iengo on data engineering, validation, tools and technologies, cybersecurity and evidence-led analysis.">
  <section class="articles">
    <header class="intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Articles</p>
      <h1>Technical work, <span class="title-accent">clear thinking.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">Articles on the technologies, design decisions and analytical questions behind my projects. Grounded in practical work, with a clear distinction between what was tested and what remains outside the evidence.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="topics" aria-label="Article topics">
      <span>Data Engineering</span><span>Tools &amp; Technologies</span><span>Cybersecurity</span><span>AI Search &amp; Research</span>
    </div>
    <section aria-labelledby="latest">
      <p class="eyebrow">Latest article</p>
      <div class="article-card">
        <div class="card-meta"><span>Data Engineering · Architecture · DuckDB</span></div>
        <h2 id="latest"><a href="/articles/what-is-duckdb/">What Is DuckDB and When Does It Make Sense?</a></h2>
        <p>An architectural assessment of embedded analytics, SQL portability and the role of independent validation alongside a managed data warehouse.</p>
        <a class="read" href="/articles/what-is-duckdb/">Read article <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="previous" aria-labelledby="previous">
      <p class="eyebrow" id="previous">Previous articles</p>
      <div class="article-card">
        <div class="card-meta"><span>Data Engineering · Data Quality · DuckDB</span><time datetime="2026-11-15">15 November 2026</time></div>
        <h2><a href="/articles/reliable-data-pipelines/">Reliable Data Pipelines Need More Than Successful Executions</a></h2>
        <p>Reproducible validation matters when analytical models become more complex. A look at what a connected DuckDB test suite can establish alongside an original Snowflake/dbt project—and where its scope ends.</p>
        <a class="read" href="/articles/reliable-data-pipelines/">Read article <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
.articles{max-width:1030px;margin:0 auto}
.intro{max-width:840px;margin-bottom:2.3rem}
.intro h1{max-width:840px}
.lead{font-size:clamp(1.07rem,2vw,1.22rem);color:#c1bdb4;max-width:760px}
.topics{display:flex;gap:.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:4.2rem}
.topics span{border:1px solid #403822;color:#D8C699;padding:.5rem .8rem;border-radius:999px;font-size:.76rem}
.previous{margin-top:3rem}
.article-card{border:1px solid #403824;border-radius:16px;background:linear-gradient(140deg,#16130e,#0b0b0b);padding:2.3rem;max-width:870px}
.card-meta{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:space-between;gap:.6rem 2rem;color:#cbb475;font-size:.77rem}
.article-card h2{margin:1.45rem 0 1rem;font-size:clamp(1.55rem,3vw,2.3rem);line-height:1.2}
.article-card h2 a{text-decoration:none}
.article-card h2 a:hover{text-decoration:underline}
.article-card p{font-size:1rem;color:#bfbab1;max-width:760px}
.read{display:inline-block;margin-top:1.25rem;color:#FFD554;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none}
.read:hover{text-decoration:underline}
@media(max-width:680px){.topics{margin-bottom:2.5rem}.article-card{padding:1.4rem}}
</style>
